                                                               Production «


                                    Why?

Kid Curry wanted this door so he could have an update made everytime
a registered S-Express user wanted the newest version of S-Express.
Of course we made it in C to accomplish some speed.

                              What does i do?

It packs n files with lha and put in to an archive defined by you. It then
gives the user a chance to download it directly.

                                 Disclaimer

We don't take any responsibility for any damage this door make on your
computer hardware or software. It has been fully tested so it shouldn't
give ya any problems.


                                Installation

You must have C:Lha so the door can pack properly.

                                  /X 2.xx

-Modify your custom-commands and add the following line:

*LHApack  XM010Doors:Lhapacker10/Lhapacker10

^         ^    ^
|         |    |_ Or wherever you put lhapacker
|         |
|         |___ Notice the "X" Lhapacker is an XIM door!
|
|______ name to be run from prompt.


                                  /X 3.xx

-Copy the icon BBS/Commands/BBsCmd/lhapacker.info to BBS/Commands/BBsCmd/
 or BBS/Commands/SysCmd/ if u don't want that LHAPacker can be runned by
 the prompt.


                               Configuration

There are som tooltypes to configurate this door with

OUTPUTLHA=<path:filename>     <--- This is the path and filename to
                                   archive that will be created
                                   (ex ram:output.lha)
                                   This archive will only be temporary
                                   and will be deleted after it's dl:ed
NAME0=<name>                  <--- Usernames allowed to use this door
.
.
NAME99=<name>

ALLNAMESALLOWED               <--- All users can use the door. This
                                   disables NAMEn=<name>

FILE0=<path:filename>         <--- Files that will be in lha-archive
.
.
.
FILE99=<path:filename>


